mode: build
flags: --optimize whole

--- OUT --->
7
7
--- IR --->
# an IR section reads main_build's dump, and `-O` above is what makes it the *optimized* release IR.
# it is spelled out because this case is the one place in the corpus that asserts what the O3 pipeline
# does to the reference counting runtime, so the optimizer is the thing under test rather than a
# background condition - it used to be implicit, because `build` optimized whether or not it was asked.
#
# and it removes all of it: the allocation, the retain for `$c = $b`, the two releases at scope end and
# the reads through the handle are all gone, and both echoes are folded to the constant 7. that is only
# sound because the counts balanced, so it is worth pinning
CHECK: i32 @main(
CHECK-NOT: call ptr @__eco_alloc
CHECK-NOT: call void @__eco_release
CHECK-NOT: strong.inc
CHECK: ret i32 0
